  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Monu S/O Siyaram Yadav And Anr vs State Of Maharashtra Thr Its Pso., Ps ... on 16 February, 2026 1 34.ba. In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Nagpur Bench : Nagpur Criminal Application No. 118 Of 2026 Monu s/o Siyaram Yadav and anr. ..vs.. State of Maharashtra",
    "facts": "2. By way of this application, the applicant is seeking bail in connection with Crime No.1083 of 2025 registered with the Pandharkawda Police Station, Yavatmal for the offence punishable under Sections 123, 274, 275, 223 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 read with Sections 26(2), 27(3), 30(2)(a) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. 3. The FIR has been lodged by the Food Safety Officer alleging that the applicants are the driver and cleaner respectively of the truck, which was stopped by the API along with other police staff and panchas. The truck was possessing contraband article i.e. scented tobacco. worth approx Rs.45 lakhs, which they wanted to transport from Hyderabad to Indore. However, that was intercepted by the police officials and applicants were arrested. The issue is pending before the Supreme Court in respect of applicability of 2 34.ba.118.2026 Section 123 of the BNS (328 of the Indian Penal Code) before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. worth approx Rs.45 lakhs. However, the government resolution prohibits the items referred in the notification and stated that it cannot be transferred from the State of Maharashtra.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned Counsel for the applicant submits that all the offences are bailable except Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. The applicants are poor persons and are earning livelihood by driving truck therefore, the applicants deserve to be enlarged on bail. 5. On the other hand, learned APP opposes the present application by submitting that both applicants were found in possession of contraband article i.e. scented tobacco while traveling through the Maharashtra State and the same is prohibited as per Government Resolution dated 16.7.2025. The investigation is going on and main culprits are absconding. Therefore, the applicants Monu S/O Siyaram Yadav And Anr vs State Of Maharashtra Thr Its Pso., Ps ... on 16 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/24806568/ 1 may not be enlarged on bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned Counsel for the applicant submits that all the offences are bailable except Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. The applicants are poor persons and are earning livelihood by driving truck therefore, the applicants deserve to be enlarged on bail. 5. On the other hand, learned APP opposes the present application by submitting that both applicants were found in possession of contraband article i.e. scented tobacco while traveling through the Maharashtra State and the same is prohibited as per Government Resolution dated 16.7.2025. The investigation is going on and main culprits are absconding. Therefore, the applicants Monu S/O Siyaram Yadav And Anr vs State Of Maharashtra Thr Its Pso., Ps ... on 16 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/24806568/ 1 may not be enlarged on bail.",
